<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore 1996 total trade rises 5.1 pct - TDB.</title>
<headline>Singapore 1996 total trade rises 5.1 pct - TDB.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total trade grew by 5.1 percent to reach Singapore $361.5 billion in 1996, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the slower growth, as compared to 13.2 percent growth in 1995, was mainly due to a cyclical slowdown in global demand for electronics and related products.</p>
<p>All major trade components except oil trade chalked up lower growth rates, the TDB said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
